  "techniqueFacts": [
    "chuck/gravy beef is the cut in all 4 sources; connective tissue breaks down over the long low cook",
    "3 of 4 sources brown the beef in batches first; one is dump-and-go with a dry spice rub (onion/garlic/mustard powder, oregano) instead",
    "thickening splits 2/2: flour coat or stir-in early vs cornstarch slurry near the end; the slurry route is naturally gluten free",
    "gluten free build swaps in GF-labelled stock and tamari for soy sauce (1 source)",
    "quick-cooking veg (green beans, silverbeet) go in only for the last 10-60 min (3 sources)",
    "root veg added partway (last 1 h) keeps them intact on the stovetop build (1 source); slow-cooker builds load them from the start (3 sources)",
    "doneness test: beef pulls apart with a fork; extend in 20-min intervals if firm (1 source)",
    "deglaze the browning pan with water to capture fond (1 source)",
    "leftovers freeze well up to 3 months (2 sources)"
